## Security Issues Found

### 1. 🔴 Critical: SQL Injection
The most severe issue — user input is directly interpolated into the SQL query.

```javascript
// Attacker sends: /api/users/1 OR 1=1
// Resulting query: SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 1 OR 1=1
// Returns ALL users in the database
```

**Fix: Use parameterized queries**
```javascript
const query = 'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?';
db.query(query, [req.params.id])
```

---

### 2. 🔴 Critical: No Authentication or Authorization
Any unauthenticated user can query any user's data.

```javascript
// Add authentication middleware
const authenticate = require('../middleware/auth');
const authorize = require('../middleware/authorize');

app.get('/api/users/:id', authenticate, authorize, (req, res) => {
  // Only proceed if user is allowed to access this resource
});
```

---

### 3. 🟠 High: No Input Validation
The ID is never validated, allowing unexpected input types.

```javascript
const { param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.get('/api/users/:id',
  param('id').isInt({ min: 1 }).toInt(),
  (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
    }
  }
);
```

---

### 4. 🟠 High: Over-fetching Data (`SELECT *`)
Returning all columns risks exposing sensitive fields like passwords or tokens.

```javascript
// Explicitly select only needed fields
const query = 'SELECT id, name, email, created_at FROM users WHERE id = ?';
```

---

### 5. 🟡 Medium: No Error Handling
Unhandled rejections can crash the server or leak stack traces.

```javascript
db.query(query, [req.params.id])
  .then(user => {
    if (!user) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'User not found' });
    res.json(user);
  })
  .catch(err => {
    console.error(err); // Log internally, don't expose to client
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  });
```

---

### Secure Revised Version

```javascript
const { param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

app.get('/api/users/:id',
  authenticate,
  param('id').isInt({ min: 1 }).toInt(),
  async (req, res) => {
    const errors = validationResult(req);
    if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
      return res.status(400).json({ errors: errors.array() });
    }

    // Users can only access their own data (or admin can access any)
    if (req.user.id !== req.params.id && !req.user.isAdmin) {
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
    }

    try {
      const query = 'SELECT id, name, email, created_at FROM users WHERE id = ?';
      const user = await db.query(query, [req.params.id]);

      if (!user) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'User not found' });

      res.json(user);
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(err);
      res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
    }
  }
);
```

---

### Summary

| Issue | Severity | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| SQL Injection | 🔴 Critical | Full DB compromise |
| No Auth/Authz | 🔴 Critical | Unauthorized data access |
| No Input Validation | 🟠 High | Unexpected behavior |
| SELECT * | 🟠 High | Sensitive data exposure |
| No Error Handling | 🟡 Medium | Info leakage / crashes |
